-- Tests for bc-interpretation-periods.l4 (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, s 25(1), s 25(2)).
-- Each expected value was decided from the text before the file was first run. Every limb of a rule is tested on both
-- sides. A case the text does not answer is asserted as the named refusal with its message (NOTES.md, finding 2).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-periods`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-time`


§ `s 25(1) Reference day`
-- 25 (1): "In sections 25.2 to 25.4, reference day means any of the following ... (a) a specified or implied day; (b) a day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs; (c) a day on which a different period begins or ends."
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the reference day` (`A specified or implied day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the reference day` (`A day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs` (YMD 2026 4 15)) TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 4 15
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the reference day` (`A day on which a different period begins or ends` (YMD 2026 5 31)) TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(1) the reference day` `Something else` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 25(1) names three kinds of reference day and no others"
-- The definition is made "In sections 25.2 to 25.4" only.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(1) the reference day` (`A specified or implied day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 25(1) defines reference day for sections 25.2 to 25.4 only"
#ASSERT `s 25(1) a thing a period is counted from is a reference day` (`A specified or implied day` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `s 25(1) a thing a period is counted from is a reference day` (`A day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs` (YMD 2026 4 15))
#ASSERT `s 25(1) a thing a period is counted from is a reference day` (`A day on which a different period begins or ends` (YMD 2026 5 31))
-- "means any of the following" closes the list: something else is not a reference day.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(1) a thing a period is counted from is a reference day` `Something else`)

§ `s 25(2) Deeds, conveyances and other legal instruments`
-- 25 (2): "This section and sections 25.1 to 25.5 also apply to a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument unless specifically provided otherwise in the deed, conveyance or other legal instrument."
#ASSERT `s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `A deed` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `A deed` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `A conveyance` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `A conveyance` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `Another legal instrument` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `Another legal instrument` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `Not a legal instrument` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 25(2) speaks only of a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` `Not a legal instrument` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 25(2) speaks only of a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument"


§ `s 25.2(3)(a) "clear" days: which end the one-day shift moves (fork F-clear-ends)`
-- 7 days after 1 January 2026, counted under 25.2(2)(a), run from 2 January to 8 January.
#ASSERT `the span of days of a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `The reference day is before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 7, `clear` IS FALSE) EQUALS `Span of days` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2026 1 2, `last day` IS YMD 2026 1 8
-- "Clear": the module moves the end the count reaches, one day later, and leaves the beginning on the day after the reference day. The rival reading moves both ends (3 to 9 January); NOTES.md, fork F-clear-ends.
#ASSERT `the span of days of a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `The reference day is before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 7, `clear` IS TRUE) EQUALS `Span of days` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2026 1 2, `last day` IS YMD 2026 1 9
